<%#
    The button that acknowledges a page: a form, not a link. Mail scanners
    and link previews open every link in a message, and the links on the
    page it opens, and a page acknowledged by one of them would stop paging
    with nobody on it. So the page asks, and only the person's own press
    sends it. The page's token (OnCallPageLinkToken), the proof that the
    press is the person's own, rides in the form, not in the address it
    posts to. A link sent before links carried a token has none to send,
    and its press is taken while it may be (OnCallAcknowledgeLink).

    Locals: formUrl, tokenParam, token (empty for none), buttonText,
    isQuiet (optional: drawn as a link, under another button), testId
    (optional; acknowledge).
-%>
<form method="POST" action="<%= formUrl %>">
    <% if (typeof token !== 'undefined' && token) { %>
    <input type="hidden" name="<%= tokenParam %>" value="<%= token %>">
    <% } %>
    <% if (typeof isQuiet !== 'undefined' && isQuiet) { %>
    <button type="submit" data-testid="<%= typeof testId !== 'undefined' && testId ? testId : 'acknowledge' %>"
        class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-200 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-gray-900 dark:hover:text-white focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:focus:ring-offset-slate-800 focus:ring-gray-500 rounded">
        <%= buttonText %>
    </button>
    <% } else { %>
    <button type="submit" data-testid="<%= typeof testId !== 'undefined' && testId ? testId : 'acknowledge' %>"
        class="w-full flex justify-center py-2 px-4 border border-transparent rounded-md shadow-sm text-sm font-medium text-white bg-yellow-600 hover:bg-yellow-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:focus:ring-offset-slate-800 focus:ring-yellow-500">
        <%= buttonText %>
    </button>
    <% } %>
</form>
